#
# Legacy CryoFall compatibility profile. Deployment identity and runtime
# operations belong to the separately versioned deployment-instance model.
# No lifecycle, update, config-write, or backup action is exposed here.

@game-profile(id="cryofall", name="CryoFall", engine="Automaton"):

  @ports:
    @port(name="game", number=6000, protocol="UDP"):
      Default game traffic port; verified in upstream documentation and the
      disposable 1.33.1.15 listener inspection.
    @end
    @port(name="lan-discovery", number=6100, protocol="UDP"):
      Observed LAN discovery listener for the tested current Linux build.
    @end
    @port(name="lan-discovery-secondary", number=61000, protocol="UDP"):
      Also observed for LAN discovery in the tested current Linux build.
    @end
  @end

  @protocol(type="custom", variant="automaton"):
    AtomicTorch Automaton protocol over UDP; not Steam/Valve A2S query.
    No standalone status/query protocol was verified in this qualification.
  @end

  @fingerprint:
    @steam-appid(server=1061710, client=829590) @end
    @executable(name="CryoFall_Server.dll") @end
    @platform(os="linux", arch="x86_64") @end
  @end

  @config(format="xml", path="<installation>/Data/SettingsServer.xml"):
    Current server configuration is generated by the game and uses lower-case
    XML element names. The old GSA Settings.xml schema does not match it; config
    write support is intentionally unavailable pending a game-specific parser.
  @end

  @clade(inherits="gsa-game", kind="game-profile"):
    Legacy game-description compatibility only. Current Linux dedicated-server
    distribution is Steam Tool AppID 1061710 and runs the .NET 6 server DLL.
    Do not use the former Podman, profile-derived identity, update, or backup
    declarations; the independent runtime and explicit instance are separate.
  @end

@end
